<title>UK: AMSTERDAM-ROTTERDAM-ANTWERP PRODUCT STOCK LEVELS.</title>
<headline>AMSTERDAM-ROTTERDAM-ANTWERP PRODUCT STOCK LEVELS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 7/8/97		  31/7/97		9/8/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	375-400			400		   400</p>
<p>    Naphtha	   50-75			 75		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,850-1,900		    1,850		 1,600</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    300		  250-275	     375-400</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     10		    10-15		    25</p>
<p>Gasoline slightly lower reflecting outgoing cargo movements. Naphtha also slipped slightly as product moved into the Germany petrochemical industry.</p>
<p>Gas oil was active with incoming Russian cargoes offset by barge sales into Germany, Switzerland and Benelux countries. Fuel gained as incoming straight run cargoes more than offset outgoing cracked product for the bunkering market and vacumm gas oil for German refineries.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, 542 4984</p>
</text>
